Update 3.0.0:
    Feat:
        - Content split: Elementalist, Monk and Trapper ship with this module, the six other classes move to FQ Card Engine Extended
        - FQ class registry: classes are no longer hardcoded in the schema, the extended module registers its own
        - Card specializations: a card carries up to four specializations of its class, shown as a gem cut in as many facets, in the corner of its description and on the thumbnails of a deck list, where the frame also shows the class colour
        - Two new classes, Runic Warrior and Fencing Master, with their tokens, decks and illustrations
        - Every class deck reworked up to level 10 (12 for some), with 22 balance passes and a full characterisation pass
        - Neutral cards become common cards, added to the spellbooks at the right levels, up to level 20
        - White Mage gets the Haunting specialization and its ghost minion
        - Crescendo becomes a monk spell
        - FQ classes capped at level 12, level-up macros, and a level is only gained once the XP exceeds the maximum for the level
        - New illustrations for every card (18 passes)
        - Equipped weapon damage added to the cards that use it, rwak and mwak taken into account when there is no attack activity
        - Attack rolls and saving throws for cards and dnd5e activities, and a successful save protects from the card effects
        - New spell/card result window, and chat messages that put the final result first
        - Resistances, immunities, vulnerabilities and absorption for card damage and damage over turns, plus a magical damage flag
        - Advantage and disadvantage handled with two dedicated FQ statuses and the dnd5e conditions
        - Rationalized effects (earth, air, fire, curse, poison, etc.) and the new VIRUS status
        - Area targeting (circle/cone/rectangle/line) from the play dialog: the covered tokens become the targets, with their own FX
        - Target all adjacent tokens, all allies or all enemies, and the distance of each target shown in the play dialog
        - Target selection is frozen in the activity when it is used, and the token auto-rotates to face its targets
        - Opportunity attacks with the first equipped weapon and automatic damage, announced in chat, only between combatants with hit points
        - Ephemeral cards: playing one destroys it for good
        - Generated cards replace the "JSON after use": cards are generated in hand from a choice offered to the player, and can be deleted from the discard
        - A card from the hand can be duplicated
        - Cards can be retrieved from the discard or from the deck back into the hand (all of them, or a given list)
        - When the deck is empty the discard is shuffled back into it, and fatigue deals damage on every reshuffle - the Runic Warrior is the only one able to lower the fatigue score
        - Base cards become innate cards and can be deleted
        - Reactive cards can be prepared during your turn and are highlighted when they become usable
        - A replayable AUTO card is played every turn (White Mage auras)
        - Cards can drop tiles carrying walls (Frost Wall)
        - Level 0 cards are no longer mandatory, and the number of level 1 cards of the main class sets the minimum size of a deck
        - Bonus score available on every type of card
        - Formulas simplified in the card descriptions, with tooltips, and localized tooltips on the card emojis
        - Improved hit bubbles
        - Minions can be placed anywhere in an area instead of an adjacent square, with a maximum number per type and summoning buffs
        - The giant skeleton becomes the Skeleton King, buffing a single skeleton
        - Spellbook reworked as a card grid, with filters, search, preview and deck size, copies toggled from the spellbook and an extra copy on right-click
        - The spellbook opens on level-up, without populating itself
        - The discard score is gone, replaced by a UI to discard cards
        - FQ costs can be set on items and spells
        - Player rights cut to the minimum: no drag and drop from the compendiums, no card drag and drop nor item edition with limited rights, on their own characters and items too
        - The GM follows a player, and the old configuration path is gone
        - A player's toolbar resolves its own hand
        - Macros: roll the current combatant's weapon damage, use the first equipped ranged weapon (macro and HUD button), end the turn, and the natural weapon in the HUD shortcuts
        - Option to bypass the attack and damage dialogs (no armour class)
        - Token coordinates in the engine are reduced to the square holding the token centre
        - Random UAT world generator (npm run testWorld:random)
        - Death saving throws and the initiative rolled on joining combat move to FQ Enhanced Combat
    Chore:
        - Version bump 14.368 and dnd5e 6.0.3, with the compendiums migrated (DAE 14.0.14, Sequencer 4.2.3)
        - Versions aligned across FQ Card Engine, FQ Enhanced Combat and FQ Restrain Movement: the three modules are published together
        - Repository moved to the final-quest GitHub organization, with a release pipeline that lints, tests, compiles the packs and publishes the release
        - LevelDB packs are no longer versioned, only their JSON sources in packs/_source (npm run build)
        - Dual licence: MIT on the source code, all rights reserved on the Final Quest 8 content
        - A utils pack to keep the pack scripts in a single place
        - LF line endings everywhere, to match what build:json writes
        - Code audit, duplication refactor and dead code removal
        - Test world updated with the new classes
        - Class balance report (npm run report:classes) and CLASSES.md documentation
    Fix:
        - Fix the OpenDeck button in the player hand
        - Cards sorted by level then by name in the decks, and the broken button removed
        - Limiting the player rights no longer removes targeting and movement on the tokens
        - Token HUD buttons follow the rights on the token's actor
        - The damage flicker no longer leaves the token invisible
        - Ephemeral cards are destroyed at the right time and show the right card back
        - Free necromancy after the first use through a generated card
        - Instant curse: the logs it relies on do not always carry the right actors or targets
        - Empty hand shown in a generated world
        - Starter heroes: max hit points override
        - FQ resources consumed at the right time with the new bypass option, and for every activity
        - Damage formulas used when an activity has damage but no attack
        - Card descriptions resized when they overflow the frame
        - Fix Light Energy and Improved Fire Ray descriptions
        - Fix orphan translations and i18n keys
        - Fix image paths
        - The result window test no longer depends on the speed of the machine
        - Opportunity attacks: FX on the right token, and the reaction reserved to combatants

Update 2.0.2:
    Feat:
        - Card draw animation
        - Show the card on click within decks/libraries
        - Consolidated chat message (choices + results) + click -> SVG card
        - Localized card choices, translated into French
        - Show specific resources (critical, discard, etc.) in the hand or the play dialog
        - Targeting available from the play dialog, with targeting errors reported before playing the card
        - Effect dispel implementation
        - X and Y value errors (overflows) blocking before playing the card in the play dialog
    Chore:
        - Restructure and remove dead CSS code
        - Architecture refactor and pending technical todos
        - Turn all CSS colors into variables
        - Add recommendation of the "FQ Restrain movement" module
        - Remove dead code and unnecessary dependencies, simplification and factorization pass
    Fix:
        - Fix card back display in the play dialog
        - Fix create-deck macro to use the FQ owner
        - Show FX after dice rolls
        - Fix frost aura
        - GM "create all decks" macro no longer opens every deck
        - No animation when drawing base cards
        - If applyEffectsFormulas.formula equals 1, skip the roll and validate immediately
        - The play dialog now closes when another play dialog opens (targeting issue)
        - Consume FQ resources at the right time when rolling weapon damage
        - No more 'S' shown in bubbles (temporary?)
        - Fix several cards: Solar Strike, Circle Attack, Secret Weapons, Curse, Elemental Magic, Tornado, Earth Fracture
        - Variable bubble font size
        - Fix effect expiration
        - Show temporary malus/bonus or those forced to be visible

Update 2.0.1:
    Feat:
        - Default card illustration and FQ logo on pause
        - On-the-fly deck generation based on cards matching classes and levels (half the max number by default), and further decks from already generated decks
        - Add a shortcut arrow to move a card from the spellbook to the deck + grey out cards already distributed in the deck
        - Dice So Nice support: simultaneous dice rolls
    Chore:
        - Unit test coverage >50%, and >80% for utils methods
        - Non-regression tests on all game cards
        - Complete documentation of methods
        - End of Card Viewer recommendation
        - Update and pin package.json dependency versions
    Fix:
        - Fix fr.json and en.json translations
        - Fix wrong control of the Y variables
        - Fix attribute modifiers wrongly translated into French (@for -> @str)
        - Do not add the hand to the container when player rights are limited
        - Fix, for cards, the v13 -> v14 breaking change of the EffectChangeData structure
        - Fix double-counting of damage when temporary HP absorb everything
        - Prevent a crash when the xyvalue evaluation fails, returning 0 instead

Update 2.0.0:
    Feat:
        - Rework of the player hand UI
        - Add FQ resources to the player hand
        - Rework of the play-card dialog UI
        - Add FQ resources and targets to the play-card dialog
        - Show FQ resources directly in the play dialog and in the hand-container
        - Cards are generated dynamically from the FQ card form via an SVG
        - Cards have a defined class that changes the texture
        - Localization (FR and EN) of all cards
        - Rework of the illustrations of all playable cards
        - New FX handling (with JB2A) and original sounds (several sounds per damage type)
        - A passive spell can only be played once per turn
        - A base spell does not necessarily stay in hand -> coupled with replayable
        - GM macro to generate a deck with all cards
    Chore:
        - Version bump 14.365
        - Refactor FQ templates and objects wired to DND5E objects (character sheets) and Foundry (cards and decks)
        - Refactor classes and static methods to keep only the strict minimum
        - Macro to generate a deck with all cards
        - Vitest migration
    Fix:
        - Fix creation of a unique deck per player with their class cards
        - Fix minion summoning
        - Fix several cards: 'Enchanted Whip', 'Rock Throw', 'Shadow Spell'

